From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Domack <patrickdk@patrickdk.com>
Date: Sun, 08 Nov 2026 09:30:04 -0500
Subject: net: phy: realtek: add PHY statistics for RTL826x

Add ethtool PHY statistics to the RTL826x driver entries, so that
ethtool --phy-statistics shows the link quality registers of the
10GBASE-T PMA and PCS.

On the RTL8261N the useful ones are the fast retrain counts in 1.147
and the latched block lock and high BER bits in 3.33. On a unit that
drops its link, a 15 second capture caught one link partner fast
retrain while 3.33 read 0x53ff, meaning block lock lost, high BER, 19
BER counts and 255 errored blocks. 1.1 kept the PMA receive link up the
whole time, so phylib never saw the event. Both registers clear on read
and their counts stop at 31, 63 and 255. read_status() reads them on
every call and adds them to 64-bit totals.

If 3.45 reads with bit 15 set and its reserved bit 14 clear, the PHY
has the high order counters of 45.2.3.19 and 45.2.3.20, and 3.33 holds
only the low bits of two 22-bit counters. The driver then reads 3.44
and 3.45 right after each 3.33 read and adds the full values. The
standard gives 3.44 no presence bit, so the driver uses it only when
3.45 is present. The RTL8261N saturates at 255, so it has neither.

3.33 belongs to the 10GBASE-T PCS. The driver counts it only while the
link runs at 10G. At 1G and 100M that PCS has no block lock and the
register means nothing. The 802.3bz drafts reuse the neighbouring 3.32
for 2.5G and 5G, but no text at hand says the same of 3.33, so those
speeds are not counted either.

The statistics, in ethtool order:

  pcs_link_drops           reads of 3.33 with bit 15 clear or bit 14
                           set, in a link-up window at 10G
  lp_fast_retrains         sum of 1.147 bits 15:11
  ld_fast_retrains         sum of 1.147 bits 10:6
  pcs_errored_blocks       sum of 3.33 bits 7:0, with 3.45 if present,
                           link-up windows at 10G only
  pcs_ber_count            sum of 3.33 bits 13:8, with 3.44 if 3.45 is
                           present, link-up windows at 10G only
  fast_retrain_negotiated  1.147 bit 3
  fast_retrain_enabled     1.147 bit 0
  lp_tx_power_backoff_db   1.131 bits 15:13 in 2 dB steps
  ld_tx_power_backoff_db   1.131 bits 12:10 in 2 dB steps
  short_reach_mode         1.131 bit 0

The first five are counts. The other five are register state that no
other interface shows. Without the two fast retrain bits, a fast
retrain count of 0 cannot tell a quiet link from one that never
negotiated fast retrain. The backoff and short reach values are what
the next patch decides on. phylib already counts the link drops it
sees in link_down_events, so they get no statistic here.

All values are unsigned. The power backoff fields are valid only while
1.129 bit 0 is set. A total not read yet, or a value whose latest read
failed, shows ETHTOOL_STAT_NOT_SET, the U64_MAX other PHY drivers use
for this. The number of statistics never changes and get_stats()
cannot fail. The optional SNR margin, minimum margin and RX power
registers, 1.133 to 1.144, are left out. The RTL8261N returns 0x0000 in
all of them, and they would need a signed encoding.

1.1 bit 2 latches low, and phylib depends on the latch. In polling mode
genphy_c45_read_link() reads 1.1 once while the link is up, so a short
drop shows up in that one read and nowhere else. The statistics never
read 1.1.

The PCS counters also run while the link trains or is down. Both units
read 3.33 as 0x7fff after boot. A 3.33 read counts only if phylib had
the link up at 10G at the previous 3.33 read and at this one. Other
reads still clear the register, and the driver drops their counts. So
a drop phylib reports counts in link_down_events and not here.
pcs_link_drops holds the events phylib does not report. Those are PCS
events while the PMA link stays up, and in interrupt mode a PMA drop
that is over before phylib reads 1.1, where its double read reports
the link up.

In polling mode read_status() samples once a second, and get_stats()
returns those totals without reading a counter. A sample between two
polls could take a drop phylib has not yet read from 1.1 into the PCS
totals as well. In interrupt mode read_status() runs only on link
changes, so get_stats() samples too, and counts 3.33 only while 1.129
bit 0 shows the PMA link up.

This applies on top of 742 "net: phy: realtek: add 5G and 10G PHY
support" and 743 "net: phy: realtek: reset RTL8261N USXGMII SerDes on
link up", which are not in mainline yet.

Signed-off-by: Patrick Domack <patrickdk@patrickdk.com>
---
 drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek.h      |   15 ++
 drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c |  226 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 240 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek.h
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek.h
@@ -8,6 +8,20 @@
 #include "phy_patch.h"
 #include "phy_patch_rtl826x.h"
 
+struct rtl826x_stats {
+	u64 pcs_link_drops;
+	u64 lp_fast_retrains;
+	u64 ld_fast_retrains;
+	u64 pcs_errored_blocks;
+	u64 pcs_ber_count;
+	int fsrt;
+	bool fsrt_seen;
+	bool pcs_seen;
+	bool pcs_window_up;
+	bool pcs_hi_checked;
+	bool pcs_hi_present;
+};
+
 struct rtl826x_priv {
 	struct rtlgen_phy_patch_db *patch;
 	bool enable_pma_low_power:1;
@@ -15,6 +29,7 @@ struct rtl826x_priv {
 	struct delayed_work sds_work;
 	bool sds_work_disabled;
 	unsigned int sds_retries;
+	struct rtl826x_stats stats;
 };
 
 int rtl822x_hwmon_init(struct phy_device *phydev);
--- a/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
  *
  * Copyright (c) 2004 Freescale Semiconductor, Inc.
  */
+#include <linux/bitfield.h>
 #include <linux/bitops.h>
 #include <linux/crc32.h>
 #include <linux/ethtool_netlink.h>
@@ -345,6 +346,24 @@ struct rtl8261x_fw_entry {
 
 #define RTL826X_VND2_INSR			0xA43A
 
+/* IEEE 802.3 Clause 45 10GBASE-T registers not in uapi/linux/mdio.h */
+#define RTL826X_PMA_10GBT_STAT			129
+#define   RTL826X_PMA_10GBT_STAT_LP_INFO_VALID	BIT(0)
+#define RTL826X_PMA_10GBT_TXPWR_LP_PBO		GENMASK(15, 13)
+#define RTL826X_PMA_10GBT_TXPWR_LD_PBO		GENMASK(12, 10)
+#define RTL826X_PMA_10GBR_FSRT_LP_COUNT		GENMASK(15, 11)
+#define RTL826X_PMA_10GBR_FSRT_LD_COUNT		GENMASK(10, 6)
+#define RTL826X_PMA_10GBR_FSRT_NEGOTIATED	BIT(3)
+#define RTL826X_PCS_10GBRT_STAT2_BLKLK		BIT(15)
+#define RTL826X_PCS_10GBRT_STAT2_HIBER		BIT(14)
+#define RTL826X_PCS_10GBRT_BER_HI		44
+#define RTL826X_PCS_10GBRT_ERR_HI		45
+#define   RTL826X_PCS_10GBRT_ERR_HI_PRESENT	BIT(15)
+#define   RTL826X_PCS_10GBRT_ERR_HI_RSVD	BIT(14)
+#define   RTL826X_PCS_10GBRT_ERR_HI_COUNT	GENMASK(13, 0)
+
+#define RTL826X_PBO_STEP_DB			2
+
 MODULE_DESCRIPTION("Realtek PHY driver");
 MODULE_AUTHOR("Johnson Leung");
 MODULE_LICENSE("GPL");
@@ -3542,6 +3561,187 @@ static int rtl826x_config_aneg(struct ph
 	return genphy_c45_check_and_restart_aneg(phydev, changed);
 }
 
+enum rtl826x_stat_index {
+	RTL826X_STAT_PCS_LINK_DROPS,
+	RTL826X_STAT_LP_FAST_RETRAINS,
+	RTL826X_STAT_LD_FAST_RETRAINS,
+	RTL826X_STAT_PCS_ERRORED_BLOCKS,
+	RTL826X_STAT_PCS_BER_COUNT,
+	RTL826X_STAT_FAST_RETRAIN_NEGOTIATED,
+	RTL826X_STAT_FAST_RETRAIN_ENABLED,
+	RTL826X_STAT_LP_PBO,
+	RTL826X_STAT_LD_PBO,
+	RTL826X_STAT_SHORT_REACH,
+	RTL826X_STAT_COUNT,
+};
+
+static const char * const rtl826x_stat_names[RTL826X_STAT_COUNT] = {
+	[RTL826X_STAT_PCS_LINK_DROPS]		= "pcs_link_drops",
+	[RTL826X_STAT_LP_FAST_RETRAINS]		= "lp_fast_retrains",
+	[RTL826X_STAT_LD_FAST_RETRAINS]		= "ld_fast_retrains",
+	[RTL826X_STAT_PCS_ERRORED_BLOCKS]	= "pcs_errored_blocks",
+	[RTL826X_STAT_PCS_BER_COUNT]		= "pcs_ber_count",
+	[RTL826X_STAT_FAST_RETRAIN_NEGOTIATED]	= "fast_retrain_negotiated",
+	[RTL826X_STAT_FAST_RETRAIN_ENABLED]	= "fast_retrain_enabled",
+	[RTL826X_STAT_LP_PBO]			= "lp_tx_power_backoff_db",
+	[RTL826X_STAT_LD_PBO]			= "ld_tx_power_backoff_db",
+	[RTL826X_STAT_SHORT_REACH]		= "short_reach_mode",
+};
+
+struct rtl826x_stat_regs {
+	int pma_10gbt_stat;
+	int txpwr;
+};
+
+static u64 rtl826x_stat_total(bool seen, u64 total)
+{
+	return seen ? total : ETHTOOL_STAT_NOT_SET;
+}
+
+static void rtl826x_stats_fsrt(struct rtl826x_stats *st, int val)
+{
+	st->fsrt = val;
+	if (val < 0)
+		return;
+
+	st->fsrt_seen = true;
+	st->lp_fast_retrains += FIELD_GET(RTL826X_PMA_10GBR_FSRT_LP_COUNT, val);
+	st->ld_fast_retrains += FIELD_GET(RTL826X_PMA_10GBR_FSRT_LD_COUNT, val);
+}
+
+/* 3.45 is there if bit 15 reads 1 and the reserved bit 14 reads 0 */
+static bool rtl826x_stats_pcs_hi(int err_hi)
+{
+	return err_hi >= 0 && (err_hi & RTL826X_PCS_10GBRT_ERR_HI_PRESENT) &&
+	       !(err_hi & RTL826X_PCS_10GBRT_ERR_HI_RSVD);
+}
+
+static void rtl826x_stats_pcs(struct rtl826x_stats *st, int val, int ber_hi,
+			      int err_hi, bool link)
+{
+	bool window_up = st->pcs_window_up && link;
+	u64 errored, ber;
+
+	st->pcs_window_up = window_up;
+	if (val < 0)
+		return;
+
+	st->pcs_seen = true;
+	st->pcs_window_up = link;
+	if (!window_up)
+		return;
+
+	if (!(val & RTL826X_PCS_10GBRT_STAT2_BLKLK) ||
+	    (val & RTL826X_PCS_10GBRT_STAT2_HIBER))
+		st->pcs_link_drops++;
+
+	errored = FIELD_GET(MDIO_PCS_10GBRT_STAT2_ERR, val);
+	ber = FIELD_GET(MDIO_PCS_10GBRT_STAT2_BER, val);
+	if (st->pcs_hi_present) {
+		if (err_hi >= 0)
+			errored |= (u64)FIELD_GET(RTL826X_PCS_10GBRT_ERR_HI_COUNT,
+						  err_hi) << 8;
+		if (ber_hi >= 0)
+			ber |= (u64)ber_hi << 6;
+	}
+
+	st->pcs_errored_blocks += errored;
+	st->pcs_ber_count += ber;
+}
+
+static void rtl826x_stats_fill(const struct rtl826x_stats *st,
+			       const struct rtl826x_stat_regs *regs, u64 *data)
+{
+	bool fsrt = st->fsrt_seen && st->fsrt >= 0;
+	bool pbo = regs->txpwr >= 0 && regs->pma_10gbt_stat >= 0 &&
+		   (regs->pma_10gbt_stat & RTL826X_PMA_10GBT_STAT_LP_INFO_VALID);
+
+	data[RTL826X_STAT_PCS_LINK_DROPS] =
+		rtl826x_stat_total(st->pcs_seen, st->pcs_link_drops);
+	data[RTL826X_STAT_LP_FAST_RETRAINS] =
+		rtl826x_stat_total(st->fsrt_seen, st->lp_fast_retrains);
+	data[RTL826X_STAT_LD_FAST_RETRAINS] =
+		rtl826x_stat_total(st->fsrt_seen, st->ld_fast_retrains);
+	data[RTL826X_STAT_PCS_ERRORED_BLOCKS] =
+		rtl826x_stat_total(st->pcs_seen, st->pcs_errored_blocks);
+	data[RTL826X_STAT_PCS_BER_COUNT] =
+		rtl826x_stat_total(st->pcs_seen, st->pcs_ber_count);
+
+	data[RTL826X_STAT_FAST_RETRAIN_NEGOTIATED] = fsrt ?
+		!!(st->fsrt & RTL826X_PMA_10GBR_FSRT_NEGOTIATED) :
+		ETHTOOL_STAT_NOT_SET;
+	data[RTL826X_STAT_FAST_RETRAIN_ENABLED] = fsrt ?
+		!!(st->fsrt & MDIO_PMA_10GBR_FSRT_ENABLE) :
+		ETHTOOL_STAT_NOT_SET;
+
+	data[RTL826X_STAT_LP_PBO] = pbo ? RTL826X_PBO_STEP_DB *
+		FIELD_GET(RTL826X_PMA_10GBT_TXPWR_LP_PBO, regs->txpwr) :
+		ETHTOOL_STAT_NOT_SET;
+	data[RTL826X_STAT_LD_PBO] = pbo ? RTL826X_PBO_STEP_DB *
+		FIELD_GET(RTL826X_PMA_10GBT_TXPWR_LD_PBO, regs->txpwr) :
+		ETHTOOL_STAT_NOT_SET;
+	data[RTL826X_STAT_SHORT_REACH] = regs->txpwr >= 0 ?
+		!!(regs->txpwr & MDIO_PMA_10GBT_TXPWR_SHORT) :
+		ETHTOOL_STAT_NOT_SET;
+}
+
+static void rtl826x_stats_sample(struct phy_device *phydev, bool pma_up)
+{
+	struct rtl826x_priv *priv = phydev->priv;
+	struct rtl826x_stats *st = &priv->stats;
+	int val, ber_hi = -ENODATA, err_hi = -ENODATA;
+
+	val = phy_read_mmd(phydev, MDIO_MMD_PMAPMD, MDIO_PMA_10GBR_FSRT_CSR);
+	rtl826x_stats_fsrt(st, val);
+
+	val = phy_read_mmd(phydev, MDIO_MMD_PCS, MDIO_PCS_10GBRT_STAT2);
+	if (val >= 0 && !st->pcs_hi_checked) {
+		st->pcs_hi_checked = true;
+		st->pcs_hi_present =
+			rtl826x_stats_pcs_hi(phy_read_mmd(phydev, MDIO_MMD_PCS,
+							  RTL826X_PCS_10GBRT_ERR_HI));
+	}
+	if (val >= 0 && st->pcs_hi_present) {
+		ber_hi = phy_read_mmd(phydev, MDIO_MMD_PCS,
+				      RTL826X_PCS_10GBRT_BER_HI);
+		err_hi = phy_read_mmd(phydev, MDIO_MMD_PCS,
+				      RTL826X_PCS_10GBRT_ERR_HI);
+	}
+	rtl826x_stats_pcs(st, val, ber_hi, err_hi, pma_up && phydev->link &&
+			  phydev->speed == SPEED_10000);
+}
+
+static int rtl826x_get_sset_count(struct phy_device *phydev)
+{
+	return RTL826X_STAT_COUNT;
+}
+
+static void rtl826x_get_strings(struct phy_device *phydev, u8 *data)
+{
+	int i;
+
+	for (i = 0; i < RTL826X_STAT_COUNT; i++)
+		ethtool_puts(&data, rtl826x_stat_names[i]);
+}
+
+static void rtl826x_get_stats(struct phy_device *phydev,
+			      struct ethtool_stats *stats, u64 *data)
+{
+	struct rtl826x_priv *priv = phydev->priv;
+	struct rtl826x_stat_regs regs;
+
+	regs.pma_10gbt_stat = phy_read_mmd(phydev, MDIO_MMD_PMAPMD,
+					   RTL826X_PMA_10GBT_STAT);
+	regs.txpwr = phy_read_mmd(phydev, MDIO_MMD_PMAPMD,
+				  MDIO_PMA_10GBT_TXPWR);
+
+	if (!phy_polling_mode(phydev))
+		rtl826x_stats_sample(phydev, regs.pma_10gbt_stat >= 0 &&
+				     (regs.pma_10gbt_stat &
+				      RTL826X_PMA_10GBT_STAT_LP_INFO_VALID));
+	rtl826x_stats_fill(&priv->stats, &regs, data);
+}
+
 static int rtl826x_read_status(struct phy_device *phydev)
 {
 	int status;
@@ -3574,7 +3774,13 @@ static int rtl826x_read_status(struct ph
 			return ret;
 	}
 
-	return genphy_c45_read_mdix(phydev);
+	ret = genphy_c45_read_mdix(phydev);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	rtl826x_stats_sample(phydev, true);
+
+	return 0;
 }
 
 static int rtl826x_config_intr(struct phy_device *phydev)
@@ -4178,6 +4384,9 @@ static struct phy_driver realtek_drvs[]
 		.get_wol        = rtl826x_get_wol,
 		.get_tunable    = rtl826x_get_tunable,
 		.set_tunable    = rtl826x_set_tunable,
+		.get_sset_count = rtl826x_get_sset_count,
+		.get_strings    = rtl826x_get_strings,
+		.get_stats      = rtl826x_get_stats,
 	}, {
 		.name           = "RTL8254B 5Gbps PHY",
 		.config_init    = rtl826x_config_init,
@@ -4195,6 +4404,9 @@ static struct phy_driver realtek_drvs[]
 		.get_wol        = rtl826x_get_wol,
 		.get_tunable    = rtl826x_get_tunable,
 		.set_tunable    = rtl826x_set_tunable,
+		.get_sset_count = rtl826x_get_sset_count,
+		.get_strings    = rtl826x_get_strings,
+		.get_stats      = rtl826x_get_stats,
 	}, {
 		.name           = "RTL8261BE 10Gbps PHY",
 		.config_init    = rtl826x_config_init,
@@ -4213,6 +4425,9 @@ static struct phy_driver realtek_drvs[]
 		.get_wol        = rtl826x_get_wol,
 		.get_tunable    = rtl826x_get_tunable,
 		.set_tunable    = rtl826x_set_tunable,
+		.get_sset_count = rtl826x_get_sset_count,
+		.get_strings    = rtl826x_get_strings,
+		.get_stats      = rtl826x_get_stats,
 	}, {
 		.name           = "RTL8261N 10Gbps PHY",
 		.config_init    = rtl826x_config_init,
@@ -4231,6 +4446,9 @@ static struct phy_driver realtek_drvs[]
 		.get_wol        = rtl826x_get_wol,
 		.get_tunable    = rtl826x_get_tunable,
 		.set_tunable    = rtl826x_set_tunable,
+		.get_sset_count = rtl826x_get_sset_count,
+		.get_strings    = rtl826x_get_strings,
+		.get_stats      = rtl826x_get_stats,
 	}, {
 		PHY_ID_MATCH_EXACT(RTL_8264),
 		.name           = "RTL8264 10Gbps PHY",
@@ -4248,6 +4466,9 @@ static struct phy_driver realtek_drvs[]
 		.get_wol        = rtl826x_get_wol,
 		.get_tunable    = rtl826x_get_tunable,
 		.set_tunable    = rtl826x_set_tunable,
+		.get_sset_count = rtl826x_get_sset_count,
+		.get_strings    = rtl826x_get_strings,
+		.get_stats      = rtl826x_get_stats,
 	}, {
 		.name           = "RTL8264B 10Gbps PHY",
 		.config_init    = rtl826x_config_init,
@@ -4265,6 +4486,9 @@ static struct phy_driver realtek_drvs[]
 		.get_wol        = rtl826x_get_wol,
 		.get_tunable    = rtl826x_get_tunable,
 		.set_tunable    = rtl826x_set_tunable,
+		.get_sset_count = rtl826x_get_sset_count,
+		.get_strings    = rtl826x_get_strings,
+		.get_stats      = rtl826x_get_stats,
 	},
 };
 
